Subject: [PATCH] feat(asks): the wave's room goes to the server's next people,
 behind a switch (BD, 1691)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

NIGHT_QUESTIONS BD, from the tester's 49931: while a wave had room, any
not-yet-asked plan person could be asked. So the model's own pick decided
who went first, and the server's order (A8, 1691) was only advice.

With WAVE_ORDER_GATE_ON, the free places of a wave go to the next people
in the server's order. Anyone else is refused, and the model reads the
drafted line, which names those people. The person the owner named is
never held back (D625), the same as at a full wave.

OFF in this commit. The line is model-facing (D44) and waits for Misho's
yes on its exact words. Turning it on is a one-line change, recorded as a §.

DONE WHEN (once on): with five plan people and a wave of three, an ask to
the fourth before the first three is refused with their names; the three
go; the owner-named person goes at any time.

